# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned it.
#
# A shell script with CRLF does not run on Linux: the interpreter reads the \r as part of
# the first argument and the file dies on its opening line — `set: Illegal option -`, which
# names neither the file nor the reason. This repository has already lost an afternoon to
# exactly that, in a container entrypoint that was fine on the machine that wrote it.
#
# So anything a Linux container executes or parses is LF, on every platform.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
